Subject: [PATCH] mtk: sched: compare the cached max clamp with UCLAMP_MAX

sched_queue_task_hook() detects clamp changes for explicitly clamped tasks.
Comparing the cached maximum against rq->uclamp[UCLAMP_MIN] produces false
positives for unchanged, non-equal clamps and misses some max-only changes.

Compare each cached clamp against the matching runqueue value. Leave the
existing enqueue guard, locking, per-CPU DVFS target and governor unchanged.

This candidate targets MTK_kernel_device_modules, not the common GKI tree.
It is not part of EVONIX's common boot image. The deployed module version,
module ABI and packaging must be validated before using a rebuilt module.

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/sched/eas/sched_main.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/sched/eas/sched_main.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/sched/eas/sched_main.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/sched/eas/sched_main.c
@@ -172,7 +172,7 @@
 
 			uclamp_diff = (uclamp_diff
 				|| (READ_ONCE(sugov_data_ptr->uclamp[UCLAMP_MAX])
-				!= READ_ONCE(rq->uclamp[UCLAMP_MIN].value)));
+				!= READ_ONCE(rq->uclamp[UCLAMP_MAX].value)));
 
 			if (uclamp_diff) {
 				int this_cpu = smp_processor_id();
